      "content": "that makes sense, i guess. but looking at the bigger picture, it feels like there's a lot of agreement that reducing car usage is basically the only way to hit climate goals. is congestion pricing seen more as a debated policy or is it pretty much just seen as the logical next step for modern cities?",
